# ESP32 Web Flasher — HTTPS frontend (issue #9, spec §7.3 of issue #3)
#
# Q1 was answered: a self-signed certificate is acceptable. We therefore use
# Caddy's internal CA (automatic HTTPS with a self-signed cert) — a valid
# secure context for the Web Serial API, and it needs no domain or DNS.
#
# To switch to a real domain + Let's Encrypt later, replace the site address
# below with your domain and remove `tls internal`. For example:
#
#     flash.example.com {
#         reverse_proxy webflasher:5060
#     }
#
# Caddy will then auto-provision and renew a Let's Encrypt certificate,
# provided DNS points at this host and ports 80/443 are reachable.

:443 {
    tls internal
    reverse_proxy webflasher:5060
}
